* DATE - DISPLAY OR SET GUEST DATE/TIME

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* DATE - DISPLAY OR SET GUEST DATE/TIME

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:DATE
    SYSUTLS:DATE SET
    SYSUTLS:DATE mm/dd/yy hh:mm:ss

Without arguments, displays the CP/M clock. DATE SET prompts for a new
date and time. The explicit date/time form sets it directly.

This controls the guest clock; it is not a macOS timezone command.
Incorrect changes can affect timestamps and bulletin-board records.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
